[39m  in the repo. There's no [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m yet, so I won't commit anything there. You may want to add [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m to one.

  The sketch shows two layouts for the filters you picked. They differ in how much JS the page needs and how big the
  diff gets:

  - [1mA. A panel always shown above the table.[0m It's a plain [38;5;153m<form method="get">[39m, so it also works with JS off. It's the
    smallest diff and uses no component variants the guidelines don't already have. The downside is that it pushes the
    table down about 150px.
  - [1mB. A compact bar, with the rest in a popover.[0m "Failed sign-ins only", a date preset and a "Filters (2)" button open
    a popover, and active filters show as removable tags. The table stays near the top. But the popover and tags need
    JS, so it still needs A's form underneath as the no-JS fallback. That roughly doubles the markup and script and gets
    close to the 300-line limit.

  I recommend [1mA[0m. The page is read-only and has at most 300 events, so it doesn't need a compact bar. A also keeps the
  no-JS rule simple to meet. We could switch to B later without changing how filtering works.

  Have a look, click one if you like, and tell me here which you prefer.

